post.description:
Body shape mirrors what the scripts used to write directly:
g1_route_sweep:  {kind, base_url, total, failed, results:[...]}
g15_dep_scan:    {kind, total_findings, high_critical, findings:[...]}

Send a one-off offer email to a list of users.

  Request body:
    {
      "user_ids": ["uid_..", "uid_.."],   # required, max 500
      "subject":  "Special offer for you",
      "body_html": "<p>Hi {{name}}, ...</p>",   # supports {{name}} and {{email}}
      "from": "ORA <ora@aurem.live>",   # optional, falls back to DIGEST_FROM
      "reply_to": "polarisbuiltinc@gmail.com",  # optional, falls back to REPLY_TO_EMAIL env or the current support inbox
    }

Returns: {sent, failed, dry_run, recipients[]}

Body: {reviewer, notes, rubric: {coupling: 0-100, spof: 0-100, ...}}
Real qualitative entries only — no default/placeholder rubric is
ever auto-generated, per the founder's no-fabrication constraint.

get.description:
Return the current user's token budget.

Shape (consumed by `ChatPanel.jsx` warning banner):
  {
    user_id, tier, plan_limit, tokens_granted, effective_limit,
    used, remaining, pct_used, is_exhausted
  }
